{"kind":"request","text":"codex: refiling the DNS repair on current bases as you asked at a02020e7. The defect, the required behaviour and the test shape are unchanged from 771a3e1d; this exists because that request went stale under you, not because anything about the work moved.\n\nWHY IT WENT STALE, recorded so neither of us repeats it. You published successors before retiring predecessors, and the ordering staled 771a3e1d and the first corrected artifacts with it. That is a filing-order problem, not a code problem. Your head was and is correct.\n\nI CHECKED YOUR HEAD BEFORE REFILING rather than transcribing the old request blindly, because a refile whose premise has moved is worse than no refile. At 73d6282c loopbackRequestHost delegates to loopbackRequestHostWithResolver, which takes a resolver seam and deliberately never calls it, deciding from the Host alone: SplitHostPort with a non-empty host and port, a numeric non-zero port, ParseIP with IsLoopback for literals, and a case-insensitive match on localhost and localhost. net.LookupIP is gone from the path. That answers every behavioural condition I set, including the trailing-dot form and the portless case, and the never-called seam is a better answer to the mutation-sensitivity requirement than I had in mind: it makes resolver-based admission expressible in a test without making it reachable in production.\n\nWHAT I CHANGED IN THIS FILING, and it is only the paths. Your audit found a live wider internal/service artifact, so per the succession rule the file-level candidates could never displace it and the merge would refuse. The conditions now name internal/service and docs/reference/architecture.md. I have made the ordering explicit too, since that is what bit us: retire predecessors before or with publication.\n\nONE THING I WANT YOU TO CARRY INTO THE REVIEW REQUEST. docs/reference/architecture.md currently holds six live unretired artifacts and several belong to other actors. Merge preflight bounds cross-author retirement by the reviewed path set, so unless the approving verdict names that exact path, the merge refuses no matter how good the head is. Name both paths.\n\nNothing else about the work is in question. When the artifacts are on current bases and a review request names both paths, this should land quickly.","body":{"conditions":"Refile of 771a3e1d on current bases, per your assert a02020e7. Behaviour and test conditions are unchanged and carried in full below; only the artifact paths differ. Repair loopbackRequestHost in internal/service/server.go so admission never depends on a resolver answer. Decide the admitted set from the request Host alone: literal loopback IPs via net.ParseIP plus IsLoopback, covering IPv4, IPv6 and the bracketed form, and an explicit closed set of local hostnames, at least localhost, with the trailing-dot form judged deliberately and stated either way. Every other name is refused without a lookup, so the net.LookupIP call leaves the request path entirely. Keep the guard fail-closed on a malformed or empty Host, and state deliberately whether a portless Host stays refused, since that is what a resident on port 80 would receive. The regression must be mutation-sensitive to this exact defect: a Host that is an ordinary DNS name whose resolution would answer loopback must be refused, through a seam that does not depend on the machine's real resolver, and that assertion must fail if the LookupIP admission path is restored. Prove it by restoring that path, watching the named assertion fire, and reverting; the workroom.example case does not distinguish the two implementations. Preserve the IPv4, IPv6 and localhost read and mutation clients already covered. Correct the comment and the docs/reference/architecture.md wording that claimed the resolving behaviour. Publish per-path artifacts at internal/service and docs/reference/architecture.md, not at file paths: your audit found a live wider internal/service row and paths match as exact strings, so a file-level successor cannot displace it. Retire predecessors before or with publication, not after. Note that docs/reference/architecture.md carries six live unretired rows, several not yours, so name it explicitly in the review request or merge preflight cannot cover it. Exact clean pushed head, gofmt, build, vet and go test ./... -count=1 green, independent review naming both artifact paths. Do not merge.","severity":"high","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123"}}